    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "`datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/` vendors the Pass 2 reference JSON and specimen (both SHA-256 locked) plus the new `barw_3d_ecm_clonal_reference.json` (SHA-256 c716e3a9..., pinned at L97 and verified fail-closed in `verify_dataset_integrity`, L127-172), with its free parameters (N_TEB, Moran rate) listed explicitly; `paper_citations.bib` adds Moran 1958 and Klein & Simons 2011 (8 entries) and the README documents the Pass 3 additions. Deductions: the Moran 1958 and Klein & Simons 2011 DOIs could not be verified offline and are flagged as such (-2); the `generation_branch_probability_profile` reference values are labelled \"obs\" without a figure-digitisation provenance (-3); the specimen's organ/stage provenance is not resolved beyond \"embryonic branched gland\" (-2); the S reference values are theoretical extremes rather than Bordeu measurements (-1)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
